; Load-time rejections of the set-level counts. Three separate kinds so
; each condition reports once against its own kind name.
;
;   `backwards`  — `:min-children` above `:max-children`. An empty range
;                  admits nothing, exactly as the per-head `:min > :max`
;                  case does.
;   `floor-sum`  — the check the *weaker* per-head spelling would let
;                  through: neither head's `:min 1` exceeds
;                  `:max-children 1`, yet satisfying both needs two
;                  children and the set allows one. Only the SUM sees it.
;   `ceil-sum`   — the mirror: `:min-children 3` above the two children
;                  its heads allow between them. Finite only because
;                  every head is bounded; one unbounded head makes the
;                  set always fillable and the check vacuous.
(plugin :name gpu :version "1.0.0"
  (form :name buffer)
  (form :name sampler)

  (value-kind :name backwards
    :underlying form
    :heads (head-set :names [buffer] :min-children 3 :max-children 1))

  (value-kind :name floor-sum
    :underlying form
    :heads (head-set :max-children 1
      (head :name buffer  :min 1)
      (head :name sampler :min 1)))

  (value-kind :name ceil-sum
    :underlying form
    :heads (head-set :min-children 3
      (head :name buffer  :max 1)
      (head :name sampler :max 1))))

; A no-op literal, not a data form: a plugin whose manifest failed to
; load is dropped entirely, so any form here would cascade into an
; `unknown_form` unrelated to what this case is about. Same reason
; `head-set-bounds-invalid` ends in a bare `42`.
42
